# What belongs in this repository: the sources, the documentation, the tools, and
# the few small files that pin the build. Everything else is either regenerable
# from those, or is content that has no business in version control.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build output
# Regenerated by `./gradlew assembleRelease`. app/build alone is ~163 MB.
build/
app/build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
app/.cxx/
.kotlin/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class

# Note on the 33 DX7 cartridges: they are NOT in this repository at all. They are
# unpacked at build time from the dexed submodule's own assets/builtin_pgm.zip
# into app/build/generated/dx7-assets/, which the build/ rules above cover.
# Dexed already publishes them; a second copy here could only drift.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ local only
# Machine-specific: sdk.dir is an absolute path on one laptop. Every checkout
# regenerates this, and committing it breaks the next machine.
local.properties
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# IDE state. Android Studio rebuilds all of it on first open.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- measurements
# Microphone captures are large, are recorded in minutes, and their CONCLUSIONS
# live in MEASUREMENTS.md, which is the part worth keeping.
captures/
*.wav
*.flac

# Instrument libraries are content, not code. Salamander alone is 1.2 GB and is a
# download, not an artefact of this project. See README.md for installing them.
# The one exception is the tiny generator-based test instrument seeded from
# assets: it is a few hundred bytes, it is the only thing that makes the audio
# path testable with no library present, and it is ours.
/instruments/
*.sfz.bak
!app/src/main/assets/instruments/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------- junk
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
